mes>D.S.</given-names></name><name><surname>Isacoff</surname><given-names>E.Y.</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Transmembrane movement of the <italic>Shaker</italic> K<sup>+</sup> channel S4</article-title><source>Neuron.</source><volume>16</volume><year>1996</year><fpage>387</fpage><lpage>397</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">8789953</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="MacKinnon1991"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>MacKinnon</surname><given-names>R.</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Determination of the subunit stoichiometry of a voltage-activated potassium channel</article-title><source>Nature.</source><volume>350</volume><year>1991</year><fpage>232</fpage><lpage>235</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">1706481</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="Mouldetal2000"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Mould</surname><given-names>J.A.</given-names></name><name><surname>Drury</surname><given-names>J.E.</given-names></name><name><surname>Frings</surname><given-names>S.M.</given-names></name><name><surname>Kaupp</surname><given-names>U.B.</given-names></name><name><surname>Pekosz</surname><given-names>A.</given-names></name><name><surname>Lamb</surname><given-names>R.A.</given-names></name><name><surname>Pinto</surname><given-names>L.H.</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Permeation and activation of the M<sub>2</sub> ion channel of influenza A virus</article-title><source>J. Biol. Chem.</source><volume>275</volume><year>2000</year><fpage>31038</fpage><lpage>31050</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">10913133</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="Nocetietal1996"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Noceti</surname><given-names>F.</given-names></name><name><surname>Baldelli</surname><given-names>P.</given-names></name><name><surname>Wei</surname><given-names>X.</given-names></nam